  "$comment": "Chain claims-sibling convention as in del-mh-001: `chain_claims` is a parallel array of decoded-claims objects for the `chain` placeholder entries; `chain_hash` is __COMPUTED_CHAIN_HASH__ (minter computes the correct §5 commitment — every signature and the hash are valid so the scope check is the isolated failure).",
  "description": "Multi-hop scope inflation (aitp/0.3 shape). chain[0] (B→C) declares scope [\"read_data\",\"admin\"], but the voucher embedded in chain[0] (A→B) granted only [\"read_data\",\"write_data\"]. The adjacent-pair scope rule (RFC-AITP-0011 §4) requires chain[0].scope ⊆ chain[0].voucher.grants; \"admin\" violates that at the voucher boundary. Every hop's JWS and the voucher are validly signed and chain_hash recomputes, and the OUTER pair check alone would pass (outer.scope [read_data] ⊆ chain[0].scope [read_data, admin]) — only checking every hop boundary, including the voucher boundary, catches the inflation. Verifier MUST reject with DELEGATION_SCOPE_EXCEEDED. Manifest source: `input.issuer_manifests` carries the signed Manifests of both hop issuers, B (kat-keypair-002, chain[0].iss) and C (kat-keypair-003, outer iss); each hop's JWS verifies under the key its issuer's Manifest designates (RFC-AITP-0011 §3 step 1). The voucher needs no Manifest: A verifies it under its own key.",
  "tags": [
    "security",
    "delegation",
    "multi-hop",
    "scope-escalation",
    "post-v0.1"
  ],
